#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550331 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca576feb-f650-5bb4-bffb-b567ff06c318" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{16{x}^{2}}{49}+\\frac{16{y}^{2}}{441}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550339}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550339} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6c9691e-11ca-5751-8436-b826f49825f6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550337}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "3bbb5303-3cd6-5c7a-94a7-126cdd38904f" :question/problem "![](images/50/50782efd1f5f15904e974810f5db14eb41ffa9a81f790226cd5048dc33c77a93.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=\\frac{7}{4}$ and the vertical radius has length $b=\\frac{21}{4}.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{\\left(\\frac{7}{4}\\right)}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{\\left(\\frac{21}{4}\\right)}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\left(\\frac{49}{16}\\right)}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{\\left(\\frac{441}{16}\\right)} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{16{x}^{2}}{49}+\\frac{16{y}^{2}}{441} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550333 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3b083f8-a5ef-562c-9608-019814b62ca2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{16{x}^{2}}{625}+\\frac{9{y}^{2}}{484}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550338}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550338} :answer-field/id #uuid "7913aa25-1f85-5a14-8bd8-8f5d63bb6afc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550336}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "4d9ef7fc-bb8c-57e4-a59a-c8e3d3a4c0d4" :question/problem "![](images/c6/c61e776c1c576b156b7fae95815459ee91b36cffd3b02ac1610a8293d9d08309.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=\\frac{25}{4}$ and the vertical radius has length $b=\\frac{22}{3}.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{\\left(\\frac{25}{4}\\right)}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{\\left(\\frac{22}{3}\\right)}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\left(\\frac{625}{16}\\right)}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{\\left(\\frac{484}{9}\\right)} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{16{x}^{2}}{625}+\\frac{9{y}^{2}}{484} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550335 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f06919c-d2d4-5cd1-ace7-b29ccdfccef1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{9{x}^{2}}{100}+\\frac{9{y}^{2}}{361}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550329}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550329} :answer-field/id #uuid "34754d1c-d6cd-5f2b-ae58-2df8c449139f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550330}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "77b4bcbd-934f-5219-bfb2-10a129134250" :question/problem "![](images/7b/7b629b57b84284cff9d54d9ac47b886be8e77c80cb1cdd3c010bf92dc16dd274.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=\\frac{10}{3}$ and the vertical radius has length $b=\\frac{19}{3}.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{\\left(\\frac{10}{3}\\right)}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{\\left(\\frac{19}{3}\\right)}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\left(\\frac{100}{9}\\right)}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{\\left(\\frac{361}{9}\\right)} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{9{x}^{2}}{100}+\\frac{9{y}^{2}}{361} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550342 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5abfe5b1-5ae6-559f-9c51-efb17e4c1804" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{9{x}^{2}}{400}+\\frac{9{y}^{2}}{529}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550334}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550334} :answer-field/id #uuid "d485f67d-1df6-51de-bddc-b8b2e1804ccd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550340}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "f3d99764-38ad-5c62-880d-420b0ba11fa5" :question/problem "![](images/f0/f0c9b9b056aa08b09342da5daad12d23c40462d25e1a04088177b51de4f9b6af.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=\\frac{20}{3}$ and the vertical radius has length $b=\\frac{23}{3}.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{\\left(\\frac{20}{3}\\right)}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{\\left(\\frac{23}{3}\\right)}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\left(\\frac{400}{9}\\right)}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{\\left(\\frac{529}{9}\\right)} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{9{x}^{2}}{400}+\\frac{9{y}^{2}}{529} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551605 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10ae2311-48e4-512d-bc98-e93ee56b201e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=C + \\frac{5 \\left(x - 4\\right)^{4}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551604} {:answer/id #uuid "296f39b6-dbd2-59f0-a5e9-b253bd51c990" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\pm \\sqrt{C - \\frac{5 \\left(x - 4\\right)^{4}}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551607} {:answer/id #uuid "4c6099ee-3b46-5070-8667-d71d5f0c9b4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=C + \\frac{\\sqrt{10} \\left(x - 4\\right)^{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551613} {:answer/id #uuid "54fc91e8-26b5-58b2-83d7-c34a6bd9e3bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\pm \\sqrt{C + 10 \\left(x - 4\\right)^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551615} {:answer/id #uuid "58c86c6d-7619-5b7c-b416-96c1c1700e10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\pm \\sqrt{C + \\frac{5 \\left(x - 4\\right)^{4}}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551617}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551617} :answer-field/id #uuid "efb1736c-eeee-5a04-88e4-57a3ff9c1730" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551642}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "16bf90c3-d378-588a-9105-03dc1e2fe7d8" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y′=\\frac{5 \\left(x - 4\\right)^{3}}{y}.$ Assume $x-4>0.$ Take both sign branches on intervals where the radicand is positive and $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y′ & =\\frac{5 \\left(x - 4\\right)^{3}}{y} \\\\ y\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} & =5 \\left(x - 4\\right)^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x & =\\int 5 \\left(x - 4\\right)^{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ \\int y\\,\\mathrm{d}y & =\\int 5 \\left(x - 4\\right)^{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ \\frac{y^{2}}{2} & =\\frac{5 \\left(x - 4\\right)^{4}}{4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\frac{y^{2}}{2}=\\frac{5 \\left(x - 4\\right)^{4}}{4}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y^2 & =\\frac{5 \\left(x - 4\\right)^{4}}{2}+2C \\\\ y & =\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac{5 \\left(x - 4\\right)^{4}}{2}+2C} \\\\ y & =\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac{5 \\left(x - 4\\right)^{4}}{2}+K}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=2C$ is an arbitrary real constant. Use either sign consistently on each interval where the radicand is positive."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551618 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d258e30-3d6d-563a-8e22-e40f19619bec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=C + \\frac{4 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551608} {:answer/id #uuid "8326b7c5-af1b-5b98-acb4-56a14bab405e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\pm \\sqrt{C - \\frac{8 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{3}}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551622} {:answer/id #uuid "8fe94f93-9195-5b19-a02c-bdfda83b3401" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\pm \\sqrt{C + 8 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551624} {:answer/id #uuid "cfd48dc4-1af4-5e7f-b474-e8e828e55194" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=C + \\frac{2 \\sqrt{6} \\sqrt{\\left(x - 3\\right)^{3}}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551634} {:answer/id #uuid "ff007452-3669-5b86-be23-b90eb6bb7e32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\pm \\sqrt{C + \\frac{8 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{3}}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551644}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551644} :answer-field/id #uuid "a37bede3-b9e4-5f1a-9f47-4fbe78c42aae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551626}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "63e2b730-0d9e-5375-bfbb-085f883671f1" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y′=\\frac{4 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{2}}{y}.$ Assume $x-3>0.$ Take both sign branches on intervals where the radicand is positive and $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y′ & =\\frac{4 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{2}}{y} \\\\ y\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} & =4 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x & =\\int 4 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ \\int y\\,\\mathrm{d}y & =\\int 4 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ \\frac{y^{2}}{2} & =\\frac{4 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{3}}{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\frac{y^{2}}{2}=\\frac{4 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{3}}{3}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y^2 & =\\frac{8 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{3}}{3}+2C \\\\ y & =\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac{8 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{3}}{3}+2C} \\\\ y & =\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac{8 \\left(x - 3\\right)^{3}}{3}+K}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=2C$ is an arbitrary real constant. Use either sign consistently on each interval where the radicand is positive."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551619 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37f4aed0-0189-5761-a8c4-d17ec0b87bfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=C + 2 e^{- 2 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551609} {:answer/id #uuid "965559e9-7c44-561c-9ece-8571d647452a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\ln{\\left(C - 2 e^{- 2 x} \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551625} {:answer/id #uuid "b419a8ce-d303-52a8-b3ae-0aa9ef7de6c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\ln{\\left(C - 4 e^{- 2 x} \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551627} {:answer/id #uuid "e20a6d5a-33a8-5f4f-9479-452bf0556b5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=C + \\ln{\\left(2 e^{- 2 x} \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551638} {:answer/id #uuid "e48d62c7-effb-500b-862f-6ecda5060a74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\ln{\\left(C + 2 e^{- 2 x} \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551639}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551639} :answer-field/id #uuid "b58179cf-e8c5-5fe4-81b8-8f5378386268" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551628}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "682503a5-3ea4-50fd-b2dd-c4f6cf554fa9" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y′=- 4 e^{- 2 x - y}.$ Work on intervals where the logarithm argument is positive." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y′ & =- 4 e^{- 2 x - y} \\\\ e^{y}\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} & =- 4 e^{- 2 x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int e^{y}\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x & =\\int - 4 e^{- 2 x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ \\int e^{y}\\,\\mathrm{d}y & =\\int - 4 e^{- 2 x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ e^{y} & =2 e^{- 2 x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\ne^{y}=2 e^{- 2 x}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\ny=\\ln{\\left(C + 2 e^{- 2 x} \\right)}.\n$$\n\nThe logarithm argument must be positive on the solution interval; $C$ is an arbitrary real constant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551620 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49b0f93b-d0f2-54df-af0f-6e0cc2394918" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\pm \\sqrt{C + \\left(x + 4\\right)^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551611} {:answer/id #uuid "c1ed890a-083e-5305-9bea-9bb4d1bea815" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=C + \\left(x + 4\\right)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551629} {:answer/id #uuid "cd687bcf-b772-5d76-b218-eacadbaa3087" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=C + \\frac{\\left(x + 4\\right)^{4}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551631} {:answer/id #uuid "ce78f957-3274-584e-a365-02e56aa1f20a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\pm \\sqrt{C - \\left(x + 4\\right)^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551632} {:answer/id #uuid "d6b9854f-6601-5d3b-be97-cf8c696cb8a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\pm \\sqrt{C + 4 \\left(x + 4\\right)^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551636}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551611} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7b6f6a4-ce2c-5b81-be6e-83b1e8a1e485" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551643}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "6fa1db63-f18e-583d-ab37-46117a1bf486" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y′=\\frac{2 \\left(x + 4\\right)^{3}}{y}.$ Assume $x+4>0.$ Take both sign branches on intervals where the radicand is positive and $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y′ & =\\frac{2 \\left(x + 4\\right)^{3}}{y} \\\\ y\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} & =2 \\left(x + 4\\right)^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x & =\\int 2 \\left(x + 4\\right)^{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ \\int y\\,\\mathrm{d}y & =\\int 2 \\left(x + 4\\right)^{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ \\frac{y^{2}}{2} & =\\frac{\\left(x + 4\\right)^{4}}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\frac{y^{2}}{2}=\\frac{\\left(x + 4\\right)^{4}}{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y^2 & =\\left(x + 4\\right)^{4}+2C \\\\ y & =\\pm\\sqrt{\\left(x + 4\\right)^{4}+2C} \\\\ y & =\\pm\\sqrt{\\left(x + 4\\right)^{4}+K}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=2C$ is an arbitrary real constant. Use either sign consistently on each interval where the radicand is positive."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551630 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f2d4e20-8550-5507-a465-b5397eb28c15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\ln{\\left(C - e^{- 2 x} \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551603} {:answer/id #uuid "1c425710-1266-581c-9722-fa8759833776" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=C + \\ln{\\left(\\frac{e^{- 2 x}}{2} \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551606} {:answer/id #uuid "4a018cae-2c2d-5c98-a82e-2dc47956d7c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\ln{\\left(C - \\frac{e^{- 2 x}}{2} \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551612} {:answer/id #uuid "55f667be-d4d4-5b14-b0fd-af942503ac45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\ln{\\left(C + \\frac{e^{- 2 x}}{2} \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551616} {:answer/id #uuid "d2892e08-e36f-52af-b525-ad4181822f25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=C + \\frac{e^{- 2 x}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551635}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551616} :answer-field/id #uuid "88407400-d880-51d2-a70f-2e5e595f4faa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551623}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "c36638cc-24f6-505b-b8ac-375828a36d26" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y′=- e^{- 2 x - y}.$ Work on intervals where the logarithm argument is positive." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y′ & =- e^{- 2 x - y} \\\\ e^{y}\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} & =- e^{- 2 x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int e^{y}\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x & =\\int - e^{- 2 x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ \\int e^{y}\\,\\mathrm{d}y & =\\int - e^{- 2 x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ e^{y} & =\\frac{e^{- 2 x}}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\ne^{y}=\\frac{e^{- 2 x}}{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\ny=\\ln{\\left(C + \\frac{e^{- 2 x}}{2} \\right)}.\n$$\n\nThe logarithm argument must be positive on the solution interval; $C$ is an arbitrary real constant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551637 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3fb015f5-5a0e-5d78-85c8-9bb2368af69d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=C + \\left(x + 7\\right)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551610} {:answer/id #uuid "50b41076-bc6b-5adf-a489-2df6a1b6896c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{C + \\left(x + 7\\right)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551614} {:answer/id #uuid "83105ce1-a627-537e-90fa-45472b86b72a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=C + \\left|{x + 7}\\right|^{\\frac{2}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551621} {:answer/id #uuid "ce90e750-d37b-538c-ba68-db863eb52201" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{C - \\left(x + 7\\right)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551633} {:answer/id #uuid "e8bad0ce-f595-50d5-af1a-7fffa40a1d48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{C + 2 x + 14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551640}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551614} :answer-field/id #uuid "eddef3a2-c678-55ce-b1af-956ae057b5f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551641}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e1bf8ae5-5934-5cc9-9596-ee1587453d65" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2(x+7)}{3{y}^{2}}.\n$$ Assume $x+7>0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2(x+7)}{3{y}^{2}} \\\\ 3{y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2(x+7)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3{y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2(x+7)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3{y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int 2(x+7)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 2(x+7)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {y}^{3} & ={(x+7)}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}={(x+7)}^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt[3]{{(x+7)}^{2}+C}.\n$$\n\nUse the real cube root, on intervals where $y\\ne 0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554780 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "053a30cb-744f-52a3-aaa9-5e9e81bf11f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K + e^{- x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554776} {:answer/id #uuid "06462b90-1d0f-5fe4-a68a-342522cfc531" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K e^{- x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554777} {:answer/id #uuid "0c2a2c6e-ec32-5cea-805b-d22ac98053a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\frac{K}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554778} {:answer/id #uuid "3bca19c9-c5ff-5a03-b2b3-062714a4d747" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K e^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554782} {:answer/id #uuid "ac436b3f-83c2-5c6e-ab75-9264f928e89f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K - x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554806}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554777} :answer-field/id #uuid "c24b3c92-af3d-5004-8811-289588535aa3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554810}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "166df804-4445-53ef-8213-cafc16efa8f7" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y'+1y=0$ for $y\\ne0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y'+1y=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+1y & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-1y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\ln|y| & =- x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\ln|y|=- x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln|y| & =- x+C \\\\ |y| & =e^{- x+C} \\\\ |y| & =e^{- x}\\cdot e^C \\\\ |y| & =K e^{- x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=e^C$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K e^{- x}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554794 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "475b7c95-614f-5077-bced-4b9b31077014" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K e^{- 6 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554785} {:answer/id #uuid "6e6219a6-d622-59d1-8986-4253dd916b77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K + e^{6 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554790} {:answer/id #uuid "945c6768-8894-517a-abc7-51f95ec1b2e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K + 6 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554800} {:answer/id #uuid "c80d4c44-6df3-5f21-80b1-61ccf01fb4a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K e^{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554812} {:answer/id #uuid "ffb372c3-9c93-5ad1-bf5a-a0b171230498" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K e^{6 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554817}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554817} :answer-field/id #uuid "740b783d-ec67-526d-a1bc-1d35f6175189" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554792}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "83abebcd-929f-55a9-a148-d27778f5afb1" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y'-6y=0$ for $y\\ne0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y'-6y=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-6y & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (6)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (6)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\ln|y| & =6 x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\ln|y|=6 x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln|y| & =6 x+C \\\\ |y| & =e^{6 x+C} \\\\ |y| & =e^{6 x}\\cdot e^C \\\\ |y| & =K e^{6 x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=e^C$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K e^{6 x}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554798 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f7b053c-d923-595c-8436-02149b0390ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K e^{2 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554783} {:answer/id #uuid "95d62561-ff51-58c3-b0d5-acccd5a59f19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K + e^{2 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554801} {:answer/id #uuid "a8de1130-c0a9-59bd-a338-4887563a0037" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K e^{- 2 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554803} {:answer/id #uuid "abb416b9-0fa8-57dd-a01e-e19606f19afd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K + 2 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554804} {:answer/id #uuid "b7f6b842-e80e-541c-9ec3-28a2725bc8b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554807}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554783} :answer-field/id #uuid "86288c86-69a9-5332-8284-b2e77b50cc38" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554795}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "927a0bdd-b0c8-54e0-a421-a7cb95e37402" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y'-2y=0$ for $y\\ne0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y'-2y=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2y & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\ln|y| & =2 x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\ln|y|=2 x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln|y| & =2 x+C \\\\ |y| & =e^{2 x+C} \\\\ |y| & =e^{2 x}\\cdot e^C \\\\ |y| & =K e^{2 x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=e^C$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K e^{2 x}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554805 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59a830d1-b55d-511e-aea9-005f1a3e7827" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K e^{\\sqrt{x^{3} + 4 x^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554787} {:answer/id #uuid "8a535be6-5fd0-59ea-93c1-018e7f1b5796" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K e^{3 x^{2} + 8 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554796} {:answer/id #uuid "8d969452-2164-5cbe-98bf-bf05149a3635" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K e^{\\sqrt{3 x^{2} + 8 x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554797} {:answer/id #uuid "929b160c-5f08-5021-837d-b9e46e9dd224" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K e^{x^{3} + 4 x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554799} {:answer/id #uuid "bf70bdc8-275d-511f-b43b-88bb3a9a1709" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K e^{6 x + 8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554808}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554799} :answer-field/id #uuid "f22ac4a5-83ff-5e96-a7cf-68957227ebfc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554816}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "abbee2f4-ef8f-5ddd-8e7c-80fb454556f0" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}-8xy=3{x}^{2}y$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}-8xy & =3{x}^{2}y \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-8xy & =3{x}^{2}y \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}y+8xy \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(3{x}^{2}+8x)y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}+8x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3{x}^{2}+8x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (3{x}^{2}+8x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & ={x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|={x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & ={x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+C \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554809 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11295145-9232-532b-9a91-62d09e45ea7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K e^{6 x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554779} {:answer/id #uuid "5c5c9f23-b6f4-5911-b0e5-a61aab827692" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K + 6 x^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554788} {:answer/id #uuid "79f6e213-4523-57a9-a155-dd7c4558da22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K e^{- 6 x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554793} {:answer/id #uuid "982ff9b1-ae32-5e5a-a7dc-2b576b8754e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K e^{12 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554802} {:answer/id #uuid "c387edae-57a2-5e79-9e57-5be3f5cdab34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K + e^{6 x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554811}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554779} :answer-field/id #uuid "7064be0c-9bce-501a-839a-b7be939751a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554791}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c07fc15d-92cf-5d4a-ac3d-da89047e596d" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y'-12 xy=0$ for $y\\ne0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y'-12 xy=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-12 xy & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =12 xy \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =12 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (12 x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (12 x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\ln|y| & =6 x^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\ln|y|=6 x^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln|y| & =6 x^{2}+C \\\\ |y| & =e^{6 x^{2}+C} \\\\ |y| & =e^{6 x^{2}}\\cdot e^C \\\\ |y| & =K e^{6 x^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=e^C$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K e^{6 x^{2}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554813 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e0c8803-ed1b-536f-b7ca-00812a0d163a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K e^{- 10 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554781} {:answer/id #uuid "426cbd07-ea11-56ec-8fa7-9cc9746a26c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K e^{5 x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554784} {:answer/id #uuid "4fc067a4-b7f1-5870-815a-7f5f267e4aa9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K - 5 x^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554786} {:answer/id #uuid "6b4e7942-9a87-59d4-aa6f-35749812b466" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K + e^{- 5 x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554789} {:answer/id #uuid "ef989fea-7778-58d0-bba3-3580cd3ba156" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K e^{- 5 x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554815}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554815} :answer-field/id #uuid "d485564e-e2b5-5d4a-867b-67459d0784ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554814}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ccb19ba7-ab90-583c-beff-0f39685096e1" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y'+10 xy=0$ for $y\\ne0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y'+10 xy=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+10 xy & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =- 10 xy \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =- 10 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (- 10 x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (- 10 x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\ln|y| & =- 5 x^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\ln|y|=- 5 x^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln|y| & =- 5 x^{2}+C \\\\ |y| & =e^{- 5 x^{2}+C} \\\\ |y| & =e^{- 5 x^{2}}\\cdot e^C \\\\ |y| & =K e^{- 5 x^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=e^C$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K e^{- 5 x^{2}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557214 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0576b7ba-7b60-5cde-90eb-b7b6e9fa9cd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2(2x-11)^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556443} {:answer/id #uuid "13af737a-117c-5f32-93ba-e6c9200ca3d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12(x-11)^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556472} {:answer/id #uuid "1fb99734-0a8c-580d-a0f8-4954f321ea9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6(2x-11)^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556506} {:answer/id #uuid "97c20d2c-d45f-5b09-9f39-ebe08248b75a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12(2x-11)^{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556794} {:answer/id #uuid "a776abf8-3706-5639-a382-e250cca33636" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12(2x-11)^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556844}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556844} :answer-field/id #uuid "9164d315-5789-5468-b831-e821976b6b32" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557148}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1b4d3073-0a5e-5d32-b8ba-a307535b4915" :question/math-academy-id "q-71958" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={(2x-11)}^{6},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=2x-11$ and $f(g(x))=g(x)^{6}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(g(x)) & =({g}^{6})^{′}=6{g}^{5}, \\\\ {g}^{′}(x) & =(2x-11)^{′}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={f}^{′}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =6{g}^{5}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =12(2x-11)^{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557259 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49385517-eeac-5b31-adab-df094762881b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556593} {:answer/id #uuid "604e0e8a-a825-50c3-a298-9ae13e709a27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556648} {:answer/id #uuid "9404be8d-cb6c-53b2-8a36-eb362e775360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556786} {:answer/id #uuid "95cb350d-4388-53ea-9992-f43b19639582" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556791} {:answer/id #uuid "9b3dc5f8-2374-5afe-8f07-96ed5f7a5da8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556807}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556593} :answer-field/id #uuid "add9725c-6d77-5248-a0ae-02fe439fa683" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557163}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "67f07fb8-cc06-5cda-9a1f-cc029f68242d" :question/math-academy-id "q-107288" :question/problem "Find the slope of the tangent to the curve $y=\\sqrt{2x+1}$ at the point where $x=4.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the slope at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nWe use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=2x+1.$ Then $y=\\sqrt{u}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2x+1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $x=4,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=4} & ={\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2x+1}}\\right)|}_{x=4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2(4)+1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557301 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c368e94-1966-5731-867b-0babe7d75b00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "36(6x-5)^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556637}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556637} :answer-field/id #uuid "258869c8-85b7-5a80-8cff-298b4785a0ca" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557088}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c1385fb4-0635-5e4c-a92d-2175e82b7bcc" :question/math-academy-id "q-314205" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={(6x-5)}^{6},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=6x-5$ and $f(g(x))=g(x)^{6}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(g(x)) & =({g}^{6})^{′}=6{g}^{5}, \\\\ {g}^{′}(x) & =(6x-5)^{′}=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={f}^{′}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =6{g}^{5}\\cdot (6) \\\\  & =36(6x-5)^{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558717 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04977381-604c-5f9d-b556-58636a85c7bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-50(T-90)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558718} {:answer/id #uuid "24b8ad68-e489-597e-b814-37c6192db3dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-90)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558725} {:answer/id #uuid "714b2ff9-4955-58ad-abdb-b041e8a8e73e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-90(T-50)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558746} {:answer/id #uuid "7629b1ef-d3ee-5ba7-9110-07ce0aa55161" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-140)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558747} {:answer/id #uuid "dda6476c-8189-5770-856f-d397f04cb065" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-50)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558761}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558761} :answer-field/id #uuid "86b8759f-3435-5375-95ee-61e854cc2d64" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558752}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "00bf0500-c9f6-5f66-b5d0-8d6213af4327" :question/problem "A medical doctor records the temperature of ${90}^{∘}\\text{F}$ using a thermometer. After the measurement is taken, the temperature reading $T(t)$ of the thermometer decreases at a rate that obeys Newton's law of cooling. Here, $T$ is measured in degrees Fahrenheit, and $t>0$ is the time in minutes. If the room temperature is ${50}^{∘}\\text{F},$ which differential equation could be used to model the thermometer reading? Assume that $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality. Write the equation in terms of the given constant $k$." :question/worked-solution "Newton's law of cooling states that the rate at which the temperature $T(t)$ of a body changes is proportional to the difference between its temperature and its surroundings. Therefore, we have the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-{T}_{S}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${T}_{S}$ is the temperature of the surroundings, and $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.\n\nIn our case, ${T}_{S}={50}^{∘}\\text{F},$ and we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-50).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558731 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "265c0696-d4ac-5159-a79f-56fe1d70bec6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-141)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558726} {:answer/id #uuid "3e20fbf0-fc4e-5883-8452-7aa1e0647b3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-90)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558733} {:answer/id #uuid "6cb67d1c-e984-5a6b-9afa-278e1bc5f857" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-51)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558745} {:answer/id #uuid "b65792e3-ac13-5cc4-9bac-39f82adb6693" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-51(T-90)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558758} {:answer/id #uuid "f8eb486c-54f5-5cc2-8c80-a61318bda736" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-90(T-51)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558762}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558745} :answer-field/id #uuid "48c21a4c-e072-51cc-9ae5-0c9beeec1bfe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558738}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3a3a9d00-f075-54dd-905e-74282fdacce0" :question/problem "A medical doctor records