roblem "The rate at which a liquid cools is proportional to the difference between its temperature and the temperature of its surroundings. Let $T(t)$ be the temperature of the liquid in degrees Celsius, and let $t>0$ be the time in minutes. If the temperature of the surroundings is ${11}^{∘}\\text{C},$ which differential equation could be used to model the temperature of the liquid? Assume that $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality. Write the equation in terms of the given constant $k$." :question/worked-solution "Newton's law of cooling states that the rate at which the temperature $T(t)$ of a body changes is proportional to the difference between its temperature and its surroundings. Therefore, we have the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-{T}_{S}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${T}_{S}$ is the temperature of the surroundings, and $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.\n\nIn our case, ${T}_{S}={11}^{∘}\\text{C},$ and we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-k(T-11).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562394 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38229b23-2b39-59e5-9abd-c6c07d94e182" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7\\cdot {4}^{7x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561722} {:answer/id #uuid "78c9ae9f-b6bd-5e2b-a491-13f9286f6a11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561883} {:answer/id #uuid "799b33bd-f993-5922-93a7-8e0d15933029" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡4\\cdot {4}^{7x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561884} {:answer/id #uuid "7ccc347a-a561-5923-a18e-8613311aa3f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{4}^{7x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561891} {:answer/id #uuid "b13acdb7-c3c6-501a-bb40-9e3bfb33ea7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7\\operatorname{ln}⁡4\\cdot {4}^{7x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562024}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562024} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc0be4a0-ce70-5992-8eed-814e9a761b79" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562341}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0876dfcc-e11e-5c1c-a9e0-0c7b6f68915a" :question/math-academy-id "q-1951" :question/problem "If $f(x)={4}^{7x},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={4}^{u},\\,u=7x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}={4}^{u}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=7.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =7\\cdot {4}^{u}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\  & =7\\operatorname{ln}⁡4\\cdot {4}^{u} \\\\  & =7\\operatorname{ln}⁡4\\cdot {4}^{7x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562416 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2dbe0539-4fe2-5131-9a91-4a158b45aa23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x{e}^{{x}^{4}+3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561701} {:answer/id #uuid "699ef952-cd7a-5cde-b182-3f4d9a8b1d58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8{x}^{3}{e}^{2{x}^{4}+3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561845} {:answer/id #uuid "7b4af48c-3147-5fd2-ba59-b1551123c8c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8x{e}^{2x+3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561887} {:answer/id #uuid "ca809957-cb8d-5918-bf34-5e74f50b4780" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5{x}^{2}{e}^{2{x}^{4}+5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562088} {:answer/id #uuid "f16911d4-15e8-5cbf-a535-476b2410db5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8x{e}^{6{x}^{4}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562184}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561845} :answer-field/id #uuid "018265d8-4b38-5450-a523-ac3f8812815c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562217}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2f55f57b-ca3e-54c4-9349-d3c4559745cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-71877" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)={e}^{2{x}^{4}+3}.$" :question/worked-solution "First we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={e}^{u},\\,u=2{x}^{4}+3.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}={e}^{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=8{x}^{3}.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{u}\\cdot (8{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =8{x}^{3}{e}^{u} \\\\  & =8{x}^{3}{e}^{2{x}^{4}+3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564735 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "108fe080-3634-56ac-a539-dec06c052af1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{3} + 3 y=- x^{3} + x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564729} {:answer/id #uuid "31d38df3-c367-5a35-814f-fb19867a0abf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{3} + 3 y=x^{3} - x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564734} {:answer/id #uuid "353ed623-65d6-5d33-a582-bf0bcd71ae20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{3} + 3 y=2 x^{3} - 2 x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564738} {:answer/id #uuid "77898ef2-efc2-5050-a06a-b026fea29a00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{3}=x^{3} - x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564757} {:answer/id #uuid "b73a7002-7a4e-5a08-b0c1-ac3576f02e1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{3} + 3 y=x^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564777}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564734} :answer-field/id #uuid "796a5d10-8fa6-5ee0-82d9-38898fc15f0d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564758}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "3215c48d-3351-57bf-9ea3-261b833ecac9" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3 x^{2} - 1}{y^{2} + 3}.\n$$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{3 x^{2} - 1}{y^{2} + 3} \\\\ (y^{2} + 3)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3 x^{2} - 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (y^{2} + 3)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3 x^{2} - 1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (y^{2} + 3)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int (3 x^{2} - 1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (y^{2} + 3)\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (3 x^{2} - 1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y^2\\,\\text{d}y+\\int 3\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 3x^2\\,\\text{d}x-\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{y^3}{3}+3y & =\\frac{3x^3}{3}-1x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\frac{y^{3}}{3} + 3 y=x^{3} - x+C.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564740 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a22c0c2-4d9d-5c18-a0b0-441ae7bb0ad3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{3}=\\frac{10 x^{3}}{3} + 2 x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564726} {:answer/id #uuid "0d13f689-3d35-5af7-b9f5-4349f82e7900" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{3}=\\frac{5 x^{3}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564727} {:answer/id #uuid "4f4b259b-6b27-5994-b54c-1fbf561a78bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{3}=- \\frac{5 x^{3}}{3} - x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564745} {:answer/id #uuid "826ec040-f791-52b3-aba7-9cd8b6d144dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{3}=\\frac{5 x^{3}}{3} + x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564764} {:answer/id #uuid "f95bd84a-b359-5bab-ac1f-d0ee64887b63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y^{2}=\\frac{5 x^{3}}{3} + x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564791}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564764} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e96b6e0-8848-548f-8b63-5f49c53df3d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564761}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3ac4a3f5-5007-54fc-9d93-b2834a665498" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{5 x^{2} + 1}{y^{2}}.\n$$ Work on an interval where $y\\ne 0.$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{5 x^{2} + 1}{y^{2}} \\\\ (y^{2})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =5 x^{2} + 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (y^{2})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (5 x^{2} + 1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (y^{2})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int (5 x^{2} + 1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (y^{2})\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (5 x^{2} + 1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y^2\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 5x^2\\,\\text{d}x+\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{y^3}{3} & =\\frac{5x^3}{3}+1x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\frac{y^{3}}{3}=\\frac{5 x^{3}}{3} + x+C.\n$$"}]}
